## What I implemented

`phone_number.py` — a `PhoneNumber` class implementing the canonical Exercism phone-number exercise (NANP):

- **`__init__(raw_input)`** — validates and normalizes:
  1. Letters → `ValueError("letters not permitted")`
  2. Disallowed punctuation (anything not `0-9 .()+ -`) → `ValueError("punctuations not permitted")`
  3. Strip non-digits; fewer than 10 → `"must not be fewer than 10 digits"`, more than 11 → `"must not be greater than 11 digits"`
  4. 11 digits must start with `1` (else `"11 digits must start with 1"`); strip the country code
  5. NXX rules: area code / exchange code can't start with `0` or `1` (exact canonical messages)
- **`number`** property — the cleaned 10-digit string
- **`area_code`** property — first 3 digits
- **`pretty()`** — `"(223)-456-7890"` format

All 4 prompt examples (`+1 (613)-995-0253`, `613-995-0253`, `1 613 995 0253`, `613.995.0253` → `6139950253`) plus the full canonical test suite are supported.

